Phase 3 polish shipped:

C1 [HIGH] — Stat component extracted:
  - apps/web/src/components/engagement/Stat.tsx (variant: plain | card)
  - 3 inline definitions removed from /engagement/page.tsx,
    /engagement/team/page.tsx, /engagement/surveys/[id]/page.tsx
  - Detail page uses variant="card" (white card wrapper)
  - Other two use variant="plain"

C2 [HIGH] — Cross-tenant ad_hoc_employee_ids guard on launch:
  - Extracted to _check_cross_tenant_ad_hoc_ids() helper
  - Applied in BOTH cohort preview AND launch handlers
  - Defense-in-depth — preview gates UI, launch gates the action

C3 [HIGH] — CSRF allowlist via settings.cors_origins:
  - _check_csrf_or_origin now compares against settings.cors_origins_list()
  - Origin: null still rejected (sandboxed iframes, file://)
  - Cross-origin Origin (e.g. attacker.com) now rejected
  - Referer fallback when Origin missing
  - Bearer-only callers (no Origin/Referer) still accepted

C8 [MEDIUM] — Test state leak fix:
  - test_submit_voided_response_returns_410 now launches its own
    fresh survey instead of relying on the shared identified_survey
    fixture. No more silent skip when test order changes.

C9 [MEDIUM] — Color tokens for engagement module:
  - Added --color-engagement-50/100/200/400/500/600/700 CSS vars
    to globals.css mirroring Tailwind's rose-* palette
  - Tailwind rose-* classes still in use (engagement is intentionally
    accent-coloured); CSS vars now available for any non-Tailwind
    consumer.

C10 [MEDIUM] — email_delivery_status set on launch (Z09 saga shape):
  - Compute partial-vs-complete from actual notification fanout count
  - Persist on EngagementSurvey row
  - Return delivery_status + delivered_count in launch response so
    UI can surface "14/28 delivered, 14 retrying" banner

4d [LOW] — Notification mark-resolved silent-swallow fix:
  - submit_my_response's mark_resolved_by_link now logs warning on
    failure instead of bare except: pass
  - Submit itself still succeeds — only the badge-dismiss is best-effort

F2.1 [LOW — doc only] — Multi-worker lock limitation comment:
  - Documented why threading.Lock is adequate for single-process
    deployments and what the Postgres advisory-lock migration looks
    like when this scales to multi-worker uvicorn

